    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 168 Whitehall Road West is an impressive 3 bedroom end of terrace home, well set back on this mature and much sought after residential road. The property has been proudly maintained and extended by the same family for 68 years and enjoys an enviable corner position on a large plot.\n\nThis impressive residence presents the lucky purchaser with a rare opportunity to acquire a well proportioned home, that also benefits from excellent scope to further extend. The ground floor comprises; a welcoming entrance hallway with a guest wc, two reception rooms and a kitchen / dining room. Upstairs there are three bedrooms and a well appointed family bathroom. There is also potential to convert the attic, as well as to extend the existing property should your needs require (subject to relevant planning permission).\n\nA description of this impressive family home would not be complete without mention of the fantastic gardens. To the front wide garden, with lawn and a cobble-lock driveway that provides ample off-off street parking and a bin-store. To the rear there is an extremely private and large garden, laid mainly in lawn and benefitting from a pathway, storage sheds and pedestrian side access. The garden also has the potential to further develop the site (subject to PP). The gardens enjoy manicured lawns, mature trees, shrubbery and hedging.\nThe location is excellent, with a wide range of everyday amenities close at hand. Local shopping is available on Whitehall Road West and Muckross Avenue, while Terenure, Sundrive, the KCR, Orwell and the Ashleaf Shopping Centre are all within easy reach, offering a broad choice of shops, cafés, bars, restaurants and services. There are also excellent recreational and sporting facilities nearby, such as the Eight Acres playing fields which as just across the road, together with a wide choice of primary and secondary schools. The area is well served by regular bus routes to the city centre and surrounding areas, while the M50 is also readily accessible.\nEarly viewing is highly recommended!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 6.48m x 3.50m\n\n\nReception Room 1 - 2.10m x 4.36m\n\n\nReception Room 2 - 4.17m x 3.65m\n\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 4.67m x 5.72m\n\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.97m x 3.48m\n\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.22m x 3.65m\n\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.89m x 2.60m\n\n\nBathroom - 2.07m x 1.65m\n\n\nWC - \n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Well appointed 3 bedroom end of terrace property </li><li>Proudly maintained and cared for by the same family for 68 years</li><li>Well set back on this mature residential road and enjoying an enviable corner site position </li><li>Ample off street parking to the front</li><li>Private and large rear garden with pedestrian side access</li><li>Potential to further extend the existing property, subject to PP</li><li>Close to a host of excellent local amenities to includes parks and playing fields, as well as primary and secondary schools </li><li>Well serviced by bus-routes and benefitting from ease of access to the m50</ul>"
      },
